[0.0, "o", "\r\n$ papertrail show 4ca1290ef789\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "                                          Attention Is All You Need                                           \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "Authors: Ashish Vaswani, Noam Shazeer, Niki Parmar, Jakob Uszkoreit, Llion Jones, Aidan N. Gomez, Lukasz      \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "Kaiser, Illia Polosukhin arXiv: 1706.03762v7 \u00b7 Published: 2017-06-12 Local model: qwen3.5:4b \u00b7 Session:       \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "4ca1290ef789                                                                                                  \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "Why this paper matters                                                                                        \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "The authors propose the Transformer, a new network architecture based solely on attention mechanisms that     \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "dispenses with recurrence and convolutions entirely. Experiments on machine translation tasks demonstrate that\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "these models are superior in quality while being more parallelizable and requiring significantly less time to \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "train. p. 1, Abstract; p. 1, Abstract                                                                         \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "Problem                                                                                                       \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "Dominant sequence transduction models rely on complex recurrent or convolutional neural networks, and to the  \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "best of the authors' knowledge, the Transformer is the first transduction model relying entirely on           \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "self-attention without using sequence-aligned RNNs or convolution. p. 1, Abstract; p. 2, 2 Background         \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "Method                                                                                                        \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", " \u2022 The Transformer follows an encoder-decoder structure using stacked self-attention and point-wise, fully    \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "   connected layers for both the encoder and decoder. p. 3, 3 Model Architecture; p. 2, 3 Model Architecture  \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", " \u2022 Source wording (automatic review requested inspection): \u201cIn the Transformer this is reduced to a constant  \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "   number of operations, albeit at the cost of reduced effective resolution due to averaging                  \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "   attention-weighted positions, an effect we counteract with Multi-Head Attention as described in section    \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "   3.2.\u201d \u201cSelf-attention, sometimes called intra-attention is an attention mechanism relating different       \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "   positions of a single sequence in order to compute a representation of the sequence.\u201d p. 2, 2 Background;  \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "   p. 2, 2 Background                                                                                         \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", " \u2022 The decoder generates an output sequence one element at a time in an auto-regressive manner, consuming     \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "   previously generated symbols as additional input. p. 2, 3 Model Architecture                               \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "Key results and claims                                                                                        \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", " \u2022 On the WMT 2014 English-to-German translation task, the model achieves a BLEU score of 28.4, and on the    \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "   English-to-French task, it establishes a new single-model state-of-the-art BLEU score of 41.8. p. 1,       \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "   Abstract; p. 1, Abstract                                                                                   \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", " \u2022 The models are more parallelizable and require significantly less time to train, and the architecture      \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "   generalizes well to other tasks such as English constituency parsing. p. 1, Abstract; p. 1, Abstract       \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", " \u2022 Training the big model on the English-to-French task took 3.5 days on eight GPUs, achieving results at less\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "   than 1/4 the training cost of the previous state-of-the-art model. p. 8, 6.1 Machine Translation; p. 8, 6.1\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "   Machine Translation                                                                                        \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "Limitations                                                                                                   \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "No explicit limitations were identified in the selected evidence; this does not establish that the paper has  \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "none.                                                                                                         \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "Suggested questions                                                                                           \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", " \u2022 How does the Transformer handle input and output modalities other than text, such as images or audio?      \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", " \u2022 What are the specific performance differences between using learned positional embeddings versus sinusoidal\r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "   positional encoding?                                                                                       \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", " \u2022 How does the model's performance scale when handling large inputs and outputs that require local,          \r\n"]
[0.691, "o", "   restricted attention mechanisms?                                                                           \r\n"]
[0.694, "o", "\r\n"]
